<title>INDIA: Indian metals' trade shut in one-day strike.</title>
<headline>Indian metals' trade shut in one-day strike.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian metals' trade was shut on Thursday in a one-day strike by traders over increased sales tax by state government authorities, dealers said.</p>
<p>On Wednesday, copper, tin and nickel prices gained. &quot;Renewed industrial buying dragged prices up while supplies of imported metals remained low,&quot; one dealer said.</p>
<p>Traders are protesting an increase in sales tax and other charges from January 1 by the government in the western Maharashtra state, where Bombay is located.</p>
<p>The markets will reopen on Friday.</p>
<p>-- Bombay Commoditiies +91-22-265 9000</p>
